# Deployment Guide for <%= projectName %>

This guide provides instructions for deploying your **<%= projectName %>** application to various production environments.

---

## 📋 Prerequisites

Before deploying, make sure you have:
1. Production environment variables configured.
2. A managed database instance ready (<%= database %>).
3. Access credentials for your hosting platform or cloud provider.

---

## ⚙️ Environment Variables

Create a `.env` file in your production environment based on `.env.example`:

```bash
PORT=<%= port || 3000 %>
NODE_ENV=production
<% if (database === 'mongodb') { %>
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://<username>:<password>@<cluster>.mongodb.net/<%= projectName %>?retryWrites=true&w=majority
<% } else if (database === 'postgres') { %>
DB_HOST=your-postgres-host.com
DB_PORT=5432
DB_USER=your_db_user
DB_PASSWORD=your_secure_password
DB_NAME=<%= projectName %>
<% } else if (database === 'mysql') { %>
DB_HOST=your-mysql-host.com
DB_PORT=3306
DB_USER=your_db_user
DB_PASSWORD=your_secure_password
DB_NAME=<%= projectName %>
<% } %>
<% if (auth === 'jwt') { %>
JWT_SECRET=your_super_secret_jwt_key_min_32_characters
JWT_EXPIRES_IN=7d
<% } %>
```

